The files listed in vendored.json (the training harness, the dilution kernels, six scripts, a smoke
config and the test fixtures) are copied from Dilution-Attention
(https://github.com/Royer-Research-Labs/Dilution-Attention, commit
144cb2d1ca4b8eef54f4de3b64d9ae3e8a8ddf68), Copyright 2026 Royer Research Labs, LLC, Apache-2.0.
The edits recorded there are import renames, the opt-in `data.bos_token` option, and 64-bit
scratch offsets in the dilution kernels. The files under results/reference/ are copied unchanged
from the same repository (results/reference/SOURCE.json).

Selective Attention is the method of Yaniv Leviathan, Matan Kalman and Yossi Matias, "Selective
Attention Improves Transformer", ICLR 2025 (arXiv:2410.02703). This repository is an independent
implementation and is not affiliated with or endorsed by the authors.
